# Line endings, pinned where they can actually break something.
#
# `deploy/deploy.sh` runs under bash on the deployment server, and the whole
# pipeline is checked out on Linux - but a Windows working copy (this project is
# developed on Windows) would otherwise turn it into CRLF, and bash reports that
# as `$'\r': command not found` on the last line: the deployment succeeds and the
# script still exits 1. Pinning these to LF removes the whole class of problem.
#
# Everything else keeps git's default behaviour.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
